in @prism
in @task
in @fractal/mandelbrot

# @task/fractal — thin bridge species composing @task with
# @fractal/mandelbrot at grep-altitude per Alex 2026-09-03 in-transcript
# ratification of Q-Mara-ε refinement: don't mint fractal-sub-graph
# semantic at @task altitude; @task family-root composes over
# @fractal/mandelbrot; @task/fractal bridge exposes the composition at
# grep-altitude for query + wire + kintsugi-sugar-desugar altitude.
#
# === Alex 2026-09-03 verbatim naming pattern ===
#
#   "There might be a @task/fractal bridge. That's a pattern we've in
#    multiple places.
#
#    Might also be something the kintsugi loop captures as a
#    collapsible sugar pattern eventually.
#
#    Like `bilateral @task @fractal` or sth like that."
#
# The bridge-species pattern (Alex 2026-09-03 verbatim: "a pattern we've
# in multiple places") captures WHERE @task-altitude composition-over-
# @fractal/mandelbrot happens at grep-altitude. Without the bridge, the
# composition lives only at @task family-root altitude and is not grep-
# visible when searching for @task ↔ @fractal composition sites.
#
# Future kintsugi collapsible sugar candidate (Alex 2026-09-03 forward-
# promised): `bilateral @task @fractal` sugar-desugar expansion where
# the kintsugi mend-loop captures the bridge-species pattern and desugars
# `bilateral @X @Y` → bridge-species shard-decl at `shards/X/Y.mirror`
# composing over `in @X + in @Y`. Species-mint gets automated at the
# kintsugi loop altitude when the pattern surfaces at scale.
#
# === The disposition ===
#
# Q-Mara-ε (Mara f5db42c §2.5 + 89ac1d4 §5.5) resolved per Alex
# 2026-09-03 in-transcript ratification composing FOURTH option not in
# Mara's original three-choice framing (@task/gestalt vs @task/sub_graph
# vs @task/mandelbrot): compose-over @fractal/mandelbrot at @task family-
# root altitude + thin bridge species at @task/fractal altitude for grep-
# visibility.
#
# Refuses:
#   - @task/gestalt (name collision with Alex's higher-altitude
#     @gestalt Obsidian-wiki-markdown-markup usage)
#   - @task/sub_graph (stringly-typed-adjacent naming per Alex 2026-09-03
#     terminal-form recognition "stringly typed navigation of human
#     knowledge"; substrate discipline refuses generic "sub_" + "graph"
#     naming when a substrate-decl'd carrier already exists)
#   - @task/mandelbrot (duplicates LANDED @fractal/mandelbrot per
#     substrate-already-had-the-word HARD RULE)
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
#   @prism             — five-op composition inherited
#   @task              — family-root parent
#   @fractal/mandelbrot — LANDED species-decl at shards/fractal/
#                          mandelbrot.mirror (Mara 2026-07-20; Alex
#                          2026-07-13 recognition "@fractal underlies
#                          @kintsugi/consent; mirror compiler IS a
#                          Mandelbrot set")
#
# === Composition-lineage ===
#
#   Mandelbrot 1980      Fractals: Form, Chance and Dimension; the
#                          mathematical substrate for fractal-recursive
#                          navigation topology
#   [[project-fractal-mandelbrot-substrate]] (Alex 2026-07-13; Rec
#                          candidate; load-bearing hinge) — @fractal
#                          underlies @kintsugi/consent + @task at every
#                          altitude
#   Rec #98 (2026-08-26; FORWARD-PROMISED) Opaque-payload-IS-fractal-
#                          AST-in-5-op-prismqueer-shape; @gestalt as
#                          bijective classifier+renderer; Rec #92
#                          Transparency<P> P-instantiated as
#                          Mandelbrot<query_AST>
#   Rec #94 (2026-08-22; MINTED) Lawvere 1969 diagonal fixed-point;
#                          the fixed-point where recursion stops moving
#                          per Alex 2026-09-01 das-Loch=das-Jetzt
#   Mara f5db42c 2026-09-02 @task canonical spec §2.5 skeleton (as
#                          @task/gestalt; refined per Alex 2026-09-03)
#   Mara 89ac1d4 2026-09-03 terminal-form spec §5.5 disposition with
#                          name-collision-warning
#   Alex 2026-09-03      Refinement resolving three-choice framing via
#                          FOURTH-option compose-over-@fractal/mandelbrot
#                          + @task/fractal thin bridge per typed-
#                          navigation recognition
#
# === Body semantics ===
#
# Every @task instance IS-A Mandelbrot<task_node> point per
# @fractal/mandelbrot mandelbrot_state variant (Liquid<task_node> in-
# flow OR Crystal<task_node> settled). @task.crystallize composes over
# @time/now.crystallize LANDED to transition Liquid → Crystal at
# temporal-singularity events.
#
# The fractal-recursion "each task contains a sub-graph that IS a task"
# (Alex 2026-09-02 verbatim; "turtles all the way down"; recursion stops
# at λ₀=NOW) IS the @fractal/mandelbrot mandelbrot_state variant applied
# recursively at task altitude.

type mandelbrot_state_of_task = ref

# === task_fractal_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Rice-safe: byte-visible mandelbrot_state variant (Liquid or Crystal)
# wrapping a well-formed task_node. Sentinel: `task=fractal-admissible`.
bilateral task_fractal_admissible {
  sentinel "task=fractal-admissible"
  arity 2
}
task_fractal_admissible(p: peer, ctx: mandelbrot_state_of_task) -> verdict { \ }

# === @task.mandelbrot_state_of — the bridge action ===
#
# Given a task_node, discharges its Mandelbrot-state per
# @fractal/mandelbrot.is_settled discipline: Crystal if the task is
# settled (content-address stable; sub-graph closed at λ₀); Liquid if
# in-flow (sub-graph in-motion; recursion not yet stopped moving).
#
# Body composes over @fractal/mandelbrot.is_settled LANDED.
#
# Sentinel: `task=mandelbrot-state-of`.
action @task.mandelbrot_state_of(t: ref) -> mandelbrot_state_of_task
  requires task_fractal_admissible(p, t)
{ \ }

out @task/fractal
out mandelbrot_state_of_task
out task_fractal_admissible
out mandelbrot_state_of
